Z||000000||turbo86se||05-27-2000||11:15 AM||||<BR>Hey guys, this doesn't happen at start up, I usually only notice this when I'm pulling my 86SE V6 into the garage. When in drive, I hear a static sound from the transmission. If I put it in reverse or nuetral, it disappears. Any ideas what it could be? <BR>This is my 2nd transmission, 15K miles on it from an 88 Formula (turbo's are hard on auto tranny's).<BR>TIA   -joel||||reg||5
Z||000001||GT Bastard||05-27-2000||04:48 PM||||What does the tranny fluid look like?  Brownish?  Burnt smelling? Anything unusual? how bout the level?  Any loose brackets in the engine bay rattling?||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||05-27-2000||09:46 PM||||Does it sound more like a high speed whine? Could be a brindled bearing. Could be evil spirits too.<P>Do you hear it if you pull it down into 1st? ||||reg||1
Z||000003||turbo86se||05-28-2000||01:16 AM||||Well, the fluid is new, and is full.  Hmm, I can't think of anything. I haven't tried putting it down into 1st, I'll try that maybe tomorrow. It definitely doesn't sound like a loose bracket, more like an electrical static noise. My tranny does not shift as firm as my 88 coupe auto, that's nice and tight. My mechanic says it's not in the best of shape. <BR>I'll have to look into this a little further later this week, thanks for the replys!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||05-28-2000||04:16 PM||||You'll likely need to get it into a good shop. It could be the thing just needs an internal adjustment. could be it's got something failing. It might not have been in real good shape when you got it.||||reg||1
